layout: template.njk
slug: estimate-hvac
title: Estimate form for HVAC (free PDF) | Jobchit
description: A free, printable HVAC estimate form. System type, equipment make and model, tons or BTU, SEER2 or AFUE, refrigerant, ducts, line set, thermostat and electrical, line items and total, with a line for the customer to sign. No account needed.
heading: Estimate for HVAC
sub: Equipment, size, efficiency, ducts and electrical on one page, with line items, a total and a line for the customer to sign when they say yes.
tips:
  - Say what the system is (central air, heat pump, furnace, mini-split or package unit) and whether it replaces old equipment or goes in new.
  - Write each piece of equipment by make, model, size (tons or BTU) and efficiency (SEER2, HSPF2 or AFUE), and say how you sized it, for example a Manual J load calculation.
  - List the duct work, line set, condensate line and pad or stand that the price covers, and the refrigerant the new system uses.
  - Note the thermostat and any electrical work, such as a new disconnect, breaker or circuit, and who removes the old unit and recovers its refrigerant.
  - Write the equipment and labor warranty terms and who pulls the permit. Put a date the price is good until, and when the customer agrees, have them sign and date it.
